    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d776">

                <pb facs="0789" n="677" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg677"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conference 184.01502/35:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Denmark</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Grant-Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Commission to Negotiate Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-23"><hi rendition="#italic">May 23,
                        1919</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received in Paris May 24, 11:10
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>383. Following from Greene, Libau.</p>
                <p>“27. May 22: As foreshadowed my telegram<anchor n="14" xml:id="d776-f1"/> general
                    offensive on against Riga; street fighting now progressing. Military authorities
                    expect to capture city not later than Sunday. Food train for city left yesterday
                    with officers A[merican] R[elief] A[dministration] and also our Mission.
                    Bolsheviki also reported attacking heavily on right flank at Bausk. See
                        Dawley report.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d776-f2"/>
                    Greene.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Grant-Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d776-f1" n="14" xml:id="d776-f1-content">
